<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayakatwang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1293">1293</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayakatwang was a ruler of Gelang-gelang in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a> and a descendant of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kediri-kingdom">Kediri</a>. In 1292 he rebelled and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kertanegara">Kertanegara</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singhasari">Singhasari</a>, reviving Kediri as the leading power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. In 1293 Kertanegara's son-in-law <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raden-wijaya">Raden Wijaya</a> joined a Mongol army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kublai-khan">Kublai Khan</a> to defeat him, then turned on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a>.</p></div>
